meta {
  name: 1 List customers (Provider role only)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/customers?page=1&pageSize=25
}
params:query {
  page: 1
  pageSize: 25
}
tests {
  test("200 for a Provider token; 403 for a Customer token", function () {
    expect([200, 403]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });
}
docs {
  **Requires the `Provider` role, not merely a token** (ADR-026, threat T-003). A `Customer`-role token
  gets `403` here by design — log in as a Provider.

  Why role-gated when the others are only authenticated: registration is anonymous and unrate-limited, so
  authentication alone would let anyone self-register as a Provider and page the entire customer table.
  **Pagination bounds the response, not the extraction.**

  ⚠️ **Known limitation, accepted:** this still returns *full* `CustomerEntity` records — including
  `subscribedProviderCollection` and `appointmentCollection`, i.e. the customer↔provider relationship
  graph. Owner-scoping to your own subscribed customers is the stronger fix and is deferred to F-021/F-024.
  This is the one exposure class F-016 closed for providers but not for customers.
}
